From 3acf61f3417f95f89d04350245af6c49808775e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc <luc@lucemans.nl>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:10:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): structure the openlv widget like the WalletConnect
 feature

- Move the widget into a lazy loaded feature behind the NATIVE_OPENLV flag,
  with the same folders as `features/walletconnect`.
- Treat NATIVE_OPENLV as on in useChains, so the patched app shows the widget
  without a gateway flag. A feature flag override can still turn it off.
- Put the header icon next to the WalletConnect one through an `openLVSlot`
  in HeaderNavigation. It shows on phone widths too.
- Use the same popup parts: connection URL input, session list with
  Disconnect, hints, error message, chain switch modal.
- Send every dApp request through useSafeWalletProvider, like WalletConnect.
  Fixed texts for the EIP-1193 codes stay, and method not found is 4200.
- Let useSafeWalletProvider take the popup and chain switch stores of the
  caller, with the WalletConnect ones as the default, so a chain switch from
  openlv opens the openlv popup and always gets an answer.
- Add `openlv` analytics events next to the WalletConnect ones.
